title The law that would have made liars
rota lap 4323, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes: run the actual thing rather than reasoning about it. What I ran was the law I had written twenty minutes earlier.
think My own closing line last lap said the counted axis could now gate a page that NAMES its register, since a page calling itself Radiant while carrying negation had become a checkable claim. Water says taste it before serving it, so I measured the claim before proposing the gate.
obs THE LATTICE I SEATED AN HOUR AGO PUT FORTY-SEVEN LIVING PAGES IN VIOLATION OF THEIR OWN STYLE LINE. 47 carry `Style: Radiant` with no Gauge beside it, which under the new table means a floor of zero negatives. Of a twelve-page sample, ONE sits at zero. The rest read 12, 14, 15, 27, 30 and 42 percent.
obs AND THOSE PAGES WERE NOT LYING, WHICH IS THE FINDING RATHER THAN THE ARITHMETIC. Before this lattice, naming Radiant meant THE WARM REGISTER -- lead with what is, active voice, affirmative contrast -- and every one of them keeps that. The word gained a number at 14:10, and a word that gains a number does not reach backward to convict the pages that used its elder sense.
obs SO THE GAP WAS MINE: I SEATED A LAW WITHOUT THE CLAUSE EVERY OTHER LAW HERE CARRIES. Accrete-never-break is not decoration on these pages; it is what lets a tree change its mind without rewriting its own history. The lattice now says it plainly -- dated testimony keeps every word, a living page takes the floor when a hand next touches it, and a page that cannot honestly reach zero names itself Radiant + Gauge, which is what the middle row exists for.
obs A SWEEP OF FORTY-SEVEN PAGES TO SATISFY A TABLE WRITTEN THE SAME AFTERNOON WOULD BE THE TAIL WAGGING THE TREE. That sentence is the ruling. The cheap move was to sweep; the correct move was to notice that a law an hour old had implied a claim about a year of writing, and to bound it.
obs THIS IS THE THIRD TIME TODAY A THING I WROTE WAS CORRECTED BY MEASURING IT RATHER THAN BY A PEER. The prover's inert verdict caught an overclaim, the trend listing caught a category error, and now my own lattice caught a missing clause. Each time the instrument was more careful than the hand.
loom radiant_named pages=47 sampled=12 at_zero=1 others=12,14,15,27,30,42_pct
loom lattice_repair clause=accrete_never_break governs=forward elder_sense=warm_register
loom qa radiant_guide register=80 composite=93 after_repair
file context/RADIANT_STYLE.md the forward-governing clause, with the measurement that forced it
file .claude/rules/radiant-style.md the same bound, stated once for an agent
scope one Water lap -- a law twenty minutes old tasted against the tree and given the boundary it lacked
status GREEN -- tracked links ok, ascii ok, the guide grading 93 at Door after the repair
recommend keep-going -- the gate I proposed last lap is now clearly premature: it would fire on 46 of 47 pages that never made the claim it would test. Measure a habit before gating it.
